{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  COOKIE CONSENT — the notice, the preferences sheet, and the "saved" line
  REFERENCE §7.9 (PHASE-2-chrome), §10 (`ag_consent`), §13 · design/CookieConsent.dc.html
  (views phone and desktop; `view=admin` is the admin console's and out of scope)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Four categories — Essential, always on, and Preferences, Analytics, Marketing — and one
  rule, owned by Services\CookiePrefs: if anything said no, the answer is no. Everything
  drawn here is `consent()`, the state CookiePrefs decided from this request in
  VisitTrackingMiddleware; this file decides nothing for itself, because a template that
  worked out whether somebody is being counted is how a page comes to tell a person the
  opposite of what is happening to them. The words for each category are
  Support\CookieRegistry::categories(), the same source as the generated half of /cookies.

  ── EVERY CONTROL IS A PLAIN FORM THAT POSTS ─────────────────────────────────

  A privacy control that needs JavaScript is missing for exactly the people likeliest to
  block it. The notice's three answers are submit buttons in one form; the sheet's
  switches are checkboxes in another. Without a script, "Choose" posts `answer=choose`,
  the server stores nothing and sends the visitor back to `#ag-consent`, and the sheet
  opens on `:target`. `consent.js` only makes the same things happen in place — a sheet
  with a focus trap that gives focus back — and is never the only way to answer.

  ── THE NOTICE'S RULES (the DC's own admin panel: "Rules the notice can't break") ──

  · Every answer carries the IDENTICAL class string — "accept is a button, decline is
    grey text" is the pattern the rules exist to stop. CookieConsentNoticeTest asserts it.
  · Nothing is switched on in advance. Preferences and Marketing start off; Analytics
    shows what is actually happening (on under the `exempt` posture, which the notice
    then says in words, off under `consent`).
  · There is no way to dismiss it without answering: no close button, no Esc.
  · It is not a modal and does not cover the tab bar — it sits above it, and the page
    keeps scroll room for it so nothing the keyboard reaches is hidden under it (2.4.11).
  · It is never drawn when the browser has already said no (GPC / DNT): asking somebody
    to agree to something we have already decided not to do is a dark pattern. The sheet,
    re-opened, says "Respected your browser's privacy signal" and offers no switch.

  Marketing is drawn as a row and has no switch: nothing on this site does marketing, and
  a switch that changes nothing is a control lying about a mechanism.
#}
{% set _c = consent() %}
{% if _c %}
{% set _counting = _c.counting %}
{% set _exempt = _c.mode == 'exempt' %}

{% if _c.ask %}
  <section class="ag-consent" role="region" aria-labelledby="ag-consent-t" data-ag-consent-bar>
    <div class="ag-consent__top">
      <span class="ag-icon-tile ag-consent__ico" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><circle cx="9" cy="10" r="1.2" fill="currentColor"></circle><circle cx="14.5" cy="14" r="1.2" fill="currentColor"></circle><circle cx="15" cy="8.5" r="1" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg></span>
      <div class="ag-consent__words">
        <h2 class="ag-consent__t" id="ag-consent-t">{{ 'Your privacy, your choice'|trans }}</h2>
        <p class="ag-consent__p">
          {{ 'Essential cookies keep you signed in.'|trans }}
          {% if _counting and not _exempt %}{{ 'With your OK we also remember your settings on this device and count visits ourselves.'|trans }}
          {% else %}{{ 'With your OK we also remember your settings on this device.'|trans }}{% endif %}
          {% if _counting and _exempt %}{{ 'We count visits ourselves unless you say no.'|trans }}{% endif %}
          {{ 'No ads, never sold.'|trans }}
          <a class="ag-consent__more" href="/cookies">{{ 'Details'|trans }}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <form class="ag-consent__answers" method="post" action="/cookies/choice">
      <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="return" value="{{ _c.return }}">
      <button class="ag-consent__answer" type="submit" name="answer" value="all">{{ 'Allow all'|trans }}</button>
      <button class="ag-consent__answer" type="submit" name="answer" value="essential">{{ 'Essential'|trans }}</button>
      <button class="ag-consent__answer" type="submit" name="answer" value="choose" data-ag-do="consent-open" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="ag-consent-sheet">{{ 'Choose'|trans }}</button>
    </form>
  </section>
{% endif %}

{% if _c.saved %}
  <div class="ag-consent-saved" role="status" data-ag-consent-saved>
    <span class="ag-consent-saved__t">
      {%- if _c.saved == 'all' %}{{ 'Saved. Everything optional is allowed.'|trans }}
      {%- elseif _c.saved == 'essential' %}{{ 'Saved. Only essential cookies are on.'|trans }}
      {%- elseif _c.saved == 'signal' %}{{ 'Saved. Your browser’s privacy signal still keeps the optional ones off.'|trans }}
      {%- else %}{{ 'Saved your choices.'|trans }}{% endif -%}
    </span>
    <a class="ag-consent-saved__change" href="#ag-consent" data-ag-do="consent-open" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="ag-consent-sheet">{{ 'Change'|trans }}</a>
  </div>
{% endif %}

{# The sheet. `#ag-consent` is its no-script door (`:target`); it is NOT `inert` in the
   markup for the same reason — a browser without the script could not lift it — and is
   hidden by the base sheet's `visibility` until it is opened. consent.js adds `inert` at
   rest, as every other sheet has. #}
<div class="ag-consent-layer" id="ag-consent">
  <div class="ag-scrim" data-ag-consent-scrim></div>
  <div class="ag-sheet ag-consent-sheet" id="ag-consent-sheet" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
       aria-labelledby="ag-consent-p" data-ag-consent-sheet>
    {# No grabber: the DC draws none, and nothing drags this sheet. #}
    <div class="ag-consent-sheet__head">
      <h2 class="ag-consent-sheet__t" id="ag-consent-p">{{ 'Your cookie choices'|trans }}</h2>
      <p class="ag-consent-sheet__sub">
        <span class="ag-consent-sheet__phone">{{ 'You can change these any time from Menu → Cookies.'|trans }}</span>
        <span class="ag-consent-sheet__wide">{{ 'You can change these any time from the Cookies page.'|trans }}</span>
      </p>
      {% if _c.signal %}
        <p class="ag-consent-sheet__signal" data-ag-consent-signal>
          <b>{{ 'Respected your browser’s privacy signal'|trans }}</b>
          {% if _c.signal == 'gpc' %}{{ 'Your browser sent Global Privacy Control, so everything optional is off. A choice made here does not overrule it.'|trans }}
          {% else %}{{ 'Your browser sent Do Not Track, so everything optional is off. A choice made here does not overrule it.'|trans }}{% endif %}
        </p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    <form class="ag-consent-sheet__form" method="post" action="/cookies/choice">
      <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="return" value="{{ _c.return }}">
      <div class="ag-consent-sheet__body">
        {% for r in _c.rows %}
          <div class="ag-consent-row">
            <span class="ag-consent-row__text">
              {% if r.kind == 'switch' %}
                <label class="ag-consent-row__name" for="ag-consent-{{ r.key }}">{{ r.name|trans }}</label>
              {% else %}
                <span class="ag-consent-row__name">{{ r.name|trans }}</span>
              {% endif %}
              <span class="ag-consent-row__desc" id="ag-consent-{{ r.key }}-d">{{ r.desc|trans }}</span>
              <span class="ag-consent-row__who">{{ r.who|trans }}</span>
            </span>
            {% if r.kind == 'switch' %}
              {# A real checkbox — it posts with the form and needs no script — laid over
                 the DC's drawn switch (52 × 32, a 26px thumb carrying On / Off) and grown
                 to a 44px target. `role="switch"` so it is announced as on/off. #}
              <span class="ag-consent-switch">
                <input class="ag-consent-switch__input" type="checkbox" role="switch" id="ag-consent-{{ r.key }}"
                       name="{{ r.key }}" value="1" aria-describedby="ag-consent-{{ r.key }}-d"{% if r.on %} checked{% endif %}>
                <span class="ag-consent-switch__track" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ag-consent-switch__thumb"><span class="ag-consent-switch__on">{{ 'On'|trans }}</span><span class="ag-consent-switch__off">{{ 'Off'|trans }}</span></span></span>
              </span>
            {% else %}
              <span class="ag-consent-row__state">
                {%- if r.kind == 'always' %}{{ 'Always on'|trans }}
                {%- elseif r.kind == 'signal' %}{{ 'Off'|trans }}
                {%- elseif r.kind == 'off_for_all' %}{{ 'Off for everyone'|trans }}
                {%- else %}{{ 'Not used'|trans }}{% endif -%}
              </span>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="ag-consent-sheet__foot">
        <button class="ag-consent-sheet__btn" type="submit" name="answer" value="essential">{{ 'Essential only'|trans }}</button>
        <button class="ag-consent-sheet__btn ag-consent-sheet__btn--save" type="submit" name="answer" value="save">{{ 'Save my choices'|trans }}</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
